MIGRATION PATH TO MODERN ALTERNATIVES
--------------------------------------

If you want to modernize further:

1. Consider mini.nvim suite:
   - mini.icons (already have) ✓
   - mini.completion (alternative to blink.cmp)
   - mini.sessions (alternative to persisted.nvim)
   - mini.files (alternative to oil.nvim)
   Benefit: Single author, consistent API, minimal

2. Replace vim.lsp.config with direct servers:
   - Current approach is already modern ✓
   - Keep as is

3. Use lazydev.nvim (already have) ✓
   - Better than neodev.nvim
   - Keep as is

4. Consider replacing autopairs:
   - mini.pairs (lighter alternative)
   - ultimate-autopair.nvim (more features)

5. Evaluate session management:
   - persisted.nvim (currently using)
   - auto-session (alternative)
   - possession.nvim (feature-rich alternative)


CUSTOMIZATION TIPS FOR DAILY USE
---------------------------------

Quick customizations without editing config:

1. Change colorscheme temporarily:
   :colorscheme habamax
   Add to local.lua to persist

2. Toggle features on the fly:
   - :TSToggle highlight (disable treesitter)
   - :set number! (toggle line numbers)
   - :set wrap! (toggle line wrap)

3. Adjust completion:
   - :set completeopt=menu,menuone,noselect
   - Adjust blink.cmp score offsets in config

4. Change LSP log level:
   - :lua vim.lsp.set_log_level('debug')
   - Check logs: :lua print(vim.lsp.get_log_path())

5. Override keymaps temporarily:
   - :nmap <key> <command>
   - Add to local.lua to persist

6. Disable plugin without restart:
   - :Lazy load plugin (load disabled plugin)
   - Can't unload, but can reload after editing

7. Change formatter on the fly:
   - :ConformInfo (see current formatter)
   - Override in buffer: vim.b.disable_autoformat = true


